      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should probably be `get_current_cred()` instead, to get the \"subjective\" (potentially overridden) creds of the current thread. Or `get_cred(filp-\u003ef_cred)`, which should be equivalent.\n\nOtherwise, if a process e.g. opens `/dev/binder` through io_uring\u0027s `IORING_OP_OPENAT`, this will get you the credentials of a kernel thread (UID 0, SELinux context `u:r:kernel:s0`).\n\n(Yes, this is a bit theoretical, since Android AFAIK doesn\u0027t have io_uring. And kernel context probably also isn\u0027t allowed to access binder anyway?)\n\n(I think the current code has the same problem.)",
      "range": {
